[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 359,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56145,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Calcifying nested stromal-epithelial tumour (CNSET) of the liver is a rare, low-grade hepatic neoplasm of uncertain lineage characterized by a distinctive nested architecture surrounded by a cellular myofibroblastic stroma and psammomatous calcifications.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 360,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56146,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 160,
        "headingText": "<p>8975/1 Calcifying nested stromal-epithelial tumour</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-11-22T17:41:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 361,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56147,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>XH8X78 Calcifying nested epithelial stromal tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 362,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56148,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> nested stromal-epithelial tumour; ossifying stromal-epithelial tumour; desmoplastic nested spindle cell tumour; ossifying malignant mixed epithelial and stromal tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 363,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56149,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 364,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56150,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNSET usually arises in the right hepatic lobe {15613852; 15613851; 19363442}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 365,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56151,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNSET is often discovered incidentally, sometimes with a history of a calcified hepatic nodule. Occasional patients present with abdominal pain, a palpable mass, or nausea. Several reported patients have presented with Cushing syndrome {15613852; 19363442}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 366,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56152,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNSET is rare, with &lt;&nbsp;40&nbsp;reported cases. There is a female predominance and a predilection for children, adolescents, and young adults {15613852; 15613851; 19363442}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 367,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56153,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most CNSETs are sporadic. Several cases have been associated with Beckwith&ndash;Wiedemann syndrome {23570373; 27965001}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 368,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56154,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>CTNNB1</em> gene deletions have been identified in several cases {22749188}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 375,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 207,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56155,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 207,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNSET is well circumscribed but unencapsulated, with a multinodular, sharp interface with adjacent liver. Tumours range from 2.8 to 30&nbsp;cm; most are &gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;cm. The cut surface is yellow or white, homogeneous, and granular {19363442}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 369,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56156,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are composed of ovoid to irregular nests of variably spindled to epithelioid cells, cuffed by a cellular stroma. A focally trabecular architecture is sometimes observed. Occasional nests contain central necrosis. The tumour cells are bland and uniform, with vesicular chromatin, indistinct nucleoli, and eosinophilic cytoplasm with low mitotic activity. The nests often harbour psammomatous calcifications, and sometimes ossification. The stroma may contain a bile ductular proliferation.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, the tumour cells are positive for broad-spectrum keratins and WT1 (usually nuclear but sometimes cytoplasmic or perinuclear dot-like), with aberrant nuclear and cytoplasmic &beta;-catenin staining {15613852; 15613851; 19363442; 22749188}. Expression of CD56, EMA, PR, neuron-specific enolase, and KIT (CD117) is variable. Desmin, chromogranin, synaptophysin, Hep&nbsp;Par-1 (CPS1), and polyclonal CEA are negative. The spindle cells in the stroma are positive for SMA.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 370,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56157,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 371,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56158,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 374,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56159,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> nested architecture surrounded by cellular myofibroblastic stroma; bland and uniform epithelioid and spindle cells; expression of keratins, WT1, and nuclear &beta;-catenin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 372,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56160,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 373,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56161,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Many patients with CNSET are cured by surgical excision, whereas several reported patients have developed locally recurrent disease, necessitating liver transplantation {15613852; 15613851; 19363442; 18338937}. One reported patient had lymph node metastasis {29290661}. Distant metastases have not been reported.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:38:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]